AB  - Voxel World Models generate sparse, game-native voxel worlds directly as editable source data. They serialize each occupied voxel as alternating position and material tokens, letting decoder-only transformers model geometry and materials without dense grids, learned 3D codebooks, or rendered-frame supervision. Decoding yields coordinate-material pairs that can be edited and scored in native sparse space. We train long-context autoregressive models on deduplicated voxel worlds and evaluate held-out completion, matched 3D-Craft completion, controls, and rendered samples. The models improve sparse completion over VoxelCNN and simple controls while preserving editable output.
